{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794173001,"nonce":"kSMkA7yrfG7QkbBzJob5V1Hw/3s=","title":"Alias lookup and duplicate consolidation pick the same copy of an external issue","message":"Found in a real Jira sync: `git work issue set \u003cKEY\u003e …` failed with \"Multiple matching issue found: \u003cid1\u003e \u003cid2\u003e\" for an issue whose second copy had already been consolidated. The quickstart promises an alias is accepted wherever an id is.\n\nThe cause is two rules for one question. Alias resolution in `cache` picks a copy by its own test (skip what is stamped `jira-consolidated-into`), and the Jira sync's consolidation picks the survivor by \"the copy that reached Jira first\". Between a pull of another clone's import and the next sync, two live copies carry the key and the lookup is ambiguous, although the sync already knows which one it will keep.\n\n## Design\n\n- One rule decides which local copy of an external issue is canonical, and both consolidation and alias resolution call it. The rule is consolidation's: the copy that reached the system first.\n- The question is backend-neutral, so it lives outside `jira` (in `cache`, beside alias resolution), and each system supplies an ordering hook. Jira registers the order it consolidates by. A system with no hook orders nothing.\n- Not \"skip archived\" or \"skip consolidated\": with the shared rule a key resolves to the right copy before consolidation has run in a clone, and resolves to the same copy after it.\n- When the rule cannot order the live copies, the lookup still fails and names every candidate id.\n- The aspect documents change in place: `doc/design/jira.md` (\"Consolidation keeps the copy that reached Jira first\") and `doc/design/cli.md` (\"A consolidated duplicate is drawn by its hash\"), plus wherever the new rule's heading belongs.\n\n## Test\n\n- Two unconsolidated copies of one Jira issue: a lookup by the key returns the copy consolidation would keep. After consolidation it returns that copy again.\n- Two live copies the rule cannot order: the lookup fails, naming both ids.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["core","bridge"],"parent":"8ade81134de7c2f5d1a16c3a48efc761b35bbf4cc2a58eaf8189fa5c15621e01","priority":"high","status":"to-do","type":"task"}}]}